{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_250","type":"reasoning","text":"Now build G03-SHA256SUMS. Note that the manifest convention (per E01/E02) excludes the manifest itself. Let me look at what E01-SHA256SUMS covers: e01-acceptance.json, e01-reliability-aggregation.md, spec, rule, lib, fixture, test. So it covers acceptance.json + doc + spec + rule + module + d.mts + test. For G03: acceptance.json, g03 doc, spec, module, d.mts, test. No rule for G03 (spec's requiredRules doesn't include a g03-specific rule). Indeed the spec requiredRules are docs-sync, agent-dev-conformance-evidence, task-forest-autoclose-and-roles, repository-artifact-retention — no new rule. Good; no new rule file.\n\nLet me write G03-SHA256SUMS in the same order and format (two spaces between hash and path).\n\nHashes:\n- g03-acceptance.json: 868cd72b8939825f9224a4c7c43f14f87cf5a8ce7896be3ec9672bfb3bfa6008\n- g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md: 2ba2f6e3938e0e3b5b6817d9af6fa6c71338f86f35921a7f08e224f9a65b23ec\n- harness spec: ec02e23816468ca305adf1aad80576f89ff389f47557aeea147ae397c7fda5cf\n- module: e7a9e7d2e3bcbe8ccb02b55b1b854e099f4c57228af246d360aaf029d1cd5c20\n- d.mts: 1d81c72959fc33944be5c0d19821ba19568a966e49516d2a54b900a28efb3f65\n- test: 5239bcc898e51d01f8fe8655379a6508ba1b5d6310433f9ea76401c0678bb264\n\nOrder matching E01-SHA256SUMS: acceptance.json, doc, spec, (rule), module, d.mts, fixture, test. I'll do: acceptance, doc, spec, module, d.mts, test. Alphabetical-ish. Let me just produce a sensible ordered list.\n\nNeed LF line endings for the manifest file. And verify with scripts/verify-evidence-sha256sums.mjs? That requires INTEGRITY.json to pick it up (it only walks manifests that have a sibling INTEGRITY.json). But acceptance criteria says \"SHA256SUMS 可回读\" (readable/verifiable). I'll verify with sha256sum -c equivalent using node, plus the repo's verify-evidence-sha256sums if it applies. Since no INTEGRITY.json exists in harness-gap-closure dir, the verify script skips those manifests... Actually verifyAllManifests filters manifests that have INTEGRITY.json. E01-SHA256SUMS is in that dir and there's no INTEGRITY.json, so it's skipped by that script. So the \"readback\" is just sha256sum -c. Let me verify by recomputing.\n\nLet me write the manifest."}}
